PATCH 456: base-loss host-pointer READ in the c00c/c035 event-post pair (asm 0xc00c/0xc035; DS=DGROUP=
0x1c00).  Both do `bx=ax; mov ax,word[bx-0x601f]` -- a DGROUP read at (param_1-0x601f) that Ghidra deref'd
as a host pointer (*(undefined2*)(param_1-0x601f)) -> the c035 SIGSEGV the b26a-corrected trajectory reaches
without setarch -R, and a wasm divergence.  Rebased the read to the DGROUP model (g_mem+0x1c000+(u16)
(param_1-0x601f)); c00c's guard made 16-bit (0xffff).  The e2c2 CALL argument is left exactly as Ghidra
emitted it (CONCAT22(param>>0x10, param_1)): the asm actually builds it from ecx/edx register math this
decompile does not model, but that expression is pure PARAMETER arithmetic -> byte-identical native<->wasm,
so it does not block byte-identity.  Its faithfulness vs the asm ecx/edx value is a separate (2da2/
faithfulness) concern, flagged not fixed here.  ASM-verified read @0xc00c/0xc035.
